WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:04.980
Dear Fellow Scholars, this is Two Minute Papers
with Dr. Károly Zsolnai-Fehér.

00:00:04.980 --> 00:00:12.249
We are back, and today we are going to marvel
at the capabilities of NVIDIA’s incredible

00:00:12.249 --> 00:00:13.379
image generation AI.

00:00:13.379 --> 00:00:18.280
And, we will see together that we can all
become witchers.

00:00:18.280 --> 00:00:25.230
Previously, they were able to create an incredible
AI that can take a piece of text from us,

00:00:25.230 --> 00:00:27.410
and create an appropriate image.

00:00:27.410 --> 00:00:33.710
Or, it could also give us a little more artistic
control as it could even transform a rough

00:00:33.710 --> 00:00:37.690
sketch into a beautiful output image.

00:00:37.690 --> 00:00:40.520
Variant generation was also possible.

00:00:40.520 --> 00:00:46.840
Or, if we didn’t feel like drawing, it could
also take segmentation maps, which specify

00:00:46.840 --> 00:00:49.170
which region should be what.

00:00:49.170 --> 00:00:53.600
The output was again, a beautiful photorealistic
image.

00:00:53.600 --> 00:00:55.540
So these were mostly landscapes.

00:00:55.540 --> 00:00:59.399
And what about human faces?

00:00:59.399 --> 00:01:02.160
Can we generate human faces too?

00:01:02.160 --> 00:01:05.600
And I wonder if we could also edit them?

00:01:05.600 --> 00:01:07.280
If so, how?

00:01:07.280 --> 00:01:13.410
Well, NVIDIA already has incredible works
for generating human faces.

00:01:13.410 --> 00:01:14.560
Look.

00:01:14.560 --> 00:01:19.950
This is their StyleGAN 3 AI, and as you see,
my goodness.

00:01:19.950 --> 00:01:27.520
These are incredible high quality faces, and
we even have a tiny bit of control over the

00:01:27.520 --> 00:01:28.520
images.

00:01:28.520 --> 00:01:32.120
Not a great deal, but a little control is
there.

00:01:32.120 --> 00:01:35.160
It works on art pieces too, by the way.

00:01:35.160 --> 00:01:40.770
And, this new technique finally gives us a
little more creative freedom in editing these

00:01:40.770 --> 00:01:43.670
images in 5 different ways.

00:01:43.670 --> 00:01:44.670
How?

00:01:44.670 --> 00:01:47.040
Well, check this out!

00:01:47.040 --> 00:01:53.800
Oh yes, one, we start sketching, and out comes
an image of this quality.

00:01:53.800 --> 00:01:54.800
Wow.

00:01:54.800 --> 00:01:59.280
This truly is a testament to the power of
AI these days.

00:01:59.280 --> 00:02:05.439
It doesn’t just generate images out of thin
air, but here, we can really harness the power

00:02:05.439 --> 00:02:12.010
of this AI and the best part is that we don’t
even need to be an expert at drawing.

00:02:12.010 --> 00:02:13.050
So cool!

00:02:13.050 --> 00:02:18.290
Two, if we don’t feel like drawing, but
we would really like to see some well-known

00:02:18.290 --> 00:02:22.790
people as cubist paintings, this can do that
too.

00:02:22.790 --> 00:02:29.730
Three, if we have an image with snow, and
we feel like chocolate, vanilla, or cherry

00:02:29.730 --> 00:02:36.120
ice cream would be so much better for snowboarding,
also, not a problem.

00:02:36.120 --> 00:02:38.000
And here comes my favorite.

00:02:38.000 --> 00:02:39.000
Four.

00:02:39.000 --> 00:02:41.750
We can make people into Witchers.

00:02:41.750 --> 00:02:44.190
I think I might make a good one.

00:02:44.190 --> 00:02:45.190
Look.

00:02:45.190 --> 00:02:52.870
This is Obi-Wan Károly, a synthetic image
of me made by an AI with an added beard.

00:02:52.870 --> 00:02:54.130
And, look.

00:02:54.130 --> 00:02:55.130
Hm-hmm!

00:02:55.130 --> 00:02:59.380
You don’t want to mess with Witcher Károly,
do you?

00:02:59.380 --> 00:03:02.980
Hmm, so who else would make a great witcher?

00:03:02.980 --> 00:03:06.160
Well, here are some of my favorites.

00:03:06.160 --> 00:03:10.180
For instance, Grimes.

00:03:10.180 --> 00:03:19.670
Beardyman, Skrillex, Robin Williams, Obama,
and The Rock.

00:03:19.670 --> 00:03:21.319
All excellent witchers!

00:03:21.319 --> 00:03:28.610
And, five, it can not only produce these images,
but even interpolate between them.

00:03:28.610 --> 00:03:29.629
What does that mean?

00:03:29.629 --> 00:03:36.680
This means that not only the final image,
but intermediate images can also be generated.

00:03:36.680 --> 00:03:43.730
Look, we are going from a photo, to a sketch,
to a Mona Lisa-style painting.

00:03:43.730 --> 00:03:49.069
While we are looking at these wonderful results,
I would like to send a huge thank you to the

00:03:49.069 --> 00:03:55.030
authors and they were very patient and took
quite a bit of time off their busy day to

00:03:55.030 --> 00:03:57.550
delight you Fellow Scholars with these animations.

00:03:57.550 --> 00:04:03.670
As a result, some of these animations you
can only see here on Two Minute Papers.

00:04:03.670 --> 00:04:05.300
That is a huge honor.

00:04:05.300 --> 00:04:06.470
Thank you so much!

00:04:06.470 --> 00:04:10.160
So, how easy it is to use?

00:04:10.160 --> 00:04:16.859
So easy that it only takes a minute to produce
such excellent results, and it likely means

00:04:16.859 --> 00:04:23.669
that this will be an excellent tool in democratizing
artistic image editing and giving it into

00:04:23.669 --> 00:04:25.629
the hands of everyone.

00:04:25.629 --> 00:04:30.550
Now make no mistake, this is a research paper,
not a product.

00:04:30.550 --> 00:04:31.550
Yet!

00:04:31.550 --> 00:04:37.409
But NVIDIA has an excellent record of transferring
these works into real products.

00:04:37.409 --> 00:04:44.990
For instance, they published a similar Audio2Face
paper in 2017, and now, just a few years later,

00:04:44.990 --> 00:04:48.150
it is out there for everyone to use.

00:04:48.150 --> 00:04:49.819
How cool is that?

00:04:49.819 --> 00:04:53.490
I really hope that this work will also have
a similar fate!

00:04:53.490 --> 00:04:55.599
What a time to be alive!

00:04:55.599 --> 00:04:58.499
So, does this get your mind going?

00:04:58.499 --> 00:05:00.150
What would you use this for?

00:05:00.150 --> 00:05:52.729
Let me know in the comments below!

00:05:52.729 --> 00:06:01.270
Thanks 
for watching and for your generous support,

00:06:01.270 --> 00:06:02.129
and I'll see you next time!

